## What happens

The test restarts the server and checks it reports `SERVING`.

Now and then it reads `NOT_SERVING` instead.

At [6351c869](https://github.com/z5labs/humus/commit/6351c86978a51659d1d1dae16a9f4553bd64a712), with go1.27.0 on 16 cores, `flaky stress` ran it 6,000 times:

|       | load 1    | load 2    |
|-------|-----------|-----------|
| cpu 1 | 0 / 1,000 | 0 / 1,000 |
| cpu 2 | 1 / 1,000 | 3 / 1,000 |
| cpu 4 | 0 / 1,000 | 2 / 1,000 |

That is 6 failures and 0 hangs. Its first failure:

```text
--- FAIL: TestServe_reports_serving/after_a_restart (0.02s)
    serve_test.go:88: got NOT_SERVING, want SERVING
```

It reproduces with:

```sh
flaky stress -tags unit -run '^TestServe_reports_serving$/^after_a_restart$' -cpu 2 -load 2 -count 1000 ./grpc/grpchealth
taskset -c 0-1 go -C grpc test -race -cover -count=1000 -cpu 2 -timeout 2m0s -run '^TestServe_reports_serving$/^after_a_restart$' ./grpchealth
```

## Why

This hasn't been triaged.

## Expected

`TestServe_reports_serving/after_a_restart` passes on every run, at every CPU count and load.

